 no idea now where this story  will take me by the time i finished  reading this arc i felt myself thinking  this more so than any other story i've  read in the past feels like a brilliant  and almost natural evolution on the  standard set by one piece and before  that dragon ball this feels like  something entirely fresh and new and i  don't really understand how best else to  express that feeling it manages to be  one of the easiest mangas i've ever read  with tremendously interesting  compositions and page layouts just like  dragon ball all the while presenting  very real and human characters i can  consider the interpersonal relationships  and intentions of like one piece this is  of course not to say that this story is  remotely like any of these properties  however the strengths that make these  stories stand out for me i feel were  inspirations for chainsaw men tatsuki  fujimoto is the youngest mangaka i've  ever covered on this channel and in  addition to that the only creator i've  ever covered that's younger than me at  28 years of age he comes from the  generation of children that grew up with  stories like one piece and naruto and he  says as much in interviews and speaking  of interviews in an interview conducted  in 2017 around the time he completed the  story of his previous series fire punch  fujimoto was asked if he considers the  reception his stories received much from  the public and to that he said  i don't think about it that much i think  my readers have read a lot of manga and  have gotten bored later in the interview  he goes on to say with the internet you  can only find what you're looking for i  like horror so i look up things about  horror but  that's totally unnecessary  you have to stray from the path if you  want to go anywhere covered clear and  obvious homages to western ideas like  zombies and stories like the texas  chainsaw massacre which fujimoto tells  us that he really likes a lot on the  very first page of the second volume  