  argue as makima cuts them off  immediately power stops shouting and  listens mahima says good girl power i  want to see big things from you and with  that very lion's completion fujimoto  brings us in for an uncomfortably  intimate close-up on makima's almost  hypnotic eye as she continues  do you think you can show me that  immediately power responds sweating uh  i'll show you this is the only  indication that something more is going  on with makima and absolutely put her on  my watch list while the rest of the  story unfolded makima is giving me mixed  vibes and signals on one hand she seems  to be held in really high regard by  pretty much everyone including aki who i  don't have a reason not to trust yet but  on the other hand she treats both denji  and power  like dogs and in response to this  supposed coercion once power learns what  denji wants she leverages that so she  can achieve her ends power wants her cat  back from this devil holding it hostage  and denji wants the goods each  individual has something the other can  potentially fulfill and therein lies the  motivation and dynamic for this short  arcs hijinx and boy does it look amazing  concerning artwork when i read the story  of one piece i loved it for its depth of  lore character and at times profound  introspection its accuracy when  dissecting the human condition through a  cavalcade of warm and fiendish  characters with chainsaw man i love it  almost as much for what amounts to  practically the exact opposite reason in  this arc i've made this argument before  much to the chagrin of the one piece  fandom but at times particularly towards  the second half of that series while oda  produces some outstanding artwork i  think he leaves a lot to be desired when  it comes to constructing and composing  his page layouts to a certain extent and  it's obviously not because he lacks the  ability he's one of the greatest to have  ever picked up the pen but what i do  think is that the depth of lore and  