 to latch  onto a dream to help him feel like part  of the group like part of the team to  feel like his life is worthwhile for his  little dog's sacrifice and while this  initial motivation is played for laughs  on a number of occasions that by the way  worked to great effect surprisingly it's  denji's reaction to his reaching of this  goal that's quite interesting with  regards to his reward from power he  feels nothing he feels hollow certainly  not the triumphant victory a typical  shonen protagonist would enjoy sitting  dejected uncertain as to whether or not  he could face reaching for another dream  out of fear of it being massively  disappointing yet again makima out of  literally nowhere fulfills this fantasy  of his and when she does  it's everything he dreamt it would be  and more  [Music]  there's a lot to unpack here within  chapter 12 there are two scenes really  two scenes that contrast heavily in  terms of tone and fujimoto wants us to  notice this shift in tone through the  words exchanged the expression shared  and indeed the framing of the two scenes  in this chapter the framing now takes  the driving seat in communicating to us  how we should understand and interpret  this story with the scene denji shares  with power in the bathroom it's framed  in a much more conventional manner as  the rest of the series bright with a few  gags and a twist at the end roll credits  right well it would be if not for the  next scene with makima for when she  shares her scene with denji everything  suddenly feels a lot more  intimate and sinister  shadows grip the pages everything that  happens is entirely by surprise or out  of control and most importantly there's  a change in physical level that reflects  that emotional reality where denji stood  above power during their scene in  makima's it's the exact opposite she  looms over his shoulder standing next to  him at first while he sits and when he  falls to the floor this divide in how  they perceive each other 